{"id": "tea:gopalatapani-upanisad:purva-2-3", "source": "src:gopalatapani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "pūrva 2-3"}, "paraphrase": "The sages ask Brahmā who is the supreme god, whom death fears; Brahmā: Kṛṣṇa (Govinda) is the supreme god; his meditation form and his mantra are given.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "teacher-transmission"], "practices": ["prc:gopala-mantra-japa"], "teachers": ["tch:brahma"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:gopalatapani-upanisad:purva-bhakti", "source": "src:gopalatapani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "pūrva (bhakti)"}, "paraphrase": "Devotion is worship of him: fixing the mind on him with no desire for this world or the next; this alone is freedom from action (naiṣkarmya).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "original": {"text": "bhaktir asya bhajanaṃ tad ihāmutropādhinairāśyenaivāmuṣmin manaḥkalpanam etad eva ca naiṣkarmyam", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Īśādiviṃśottaraśatopaniṣadaḥ (Nirṇayasāgara collection of 120 Upaniṣads), South Indian recension carrying Upaniṣad Brahmayogin's opening maṅgala verses; e-text github.com/sanskrit/raw_etexts vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md", "licence": "text public domain; e-text licence unstated"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:gopalatapani-upanisad:uttara-summary", "source": "src:gopalatapani-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "uttara (summary)"}, "paraphrase": "The gopīs ask Durvāsas; Kṛṣṇa is the Self, ever celibate though amid them; Mathurā is described as a maṇḍala; Kṛṣṇa is the one Lord in all.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "teachers": ["tch:durvasas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
